WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:02.969
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Billy Crystal.

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:04.237
You were saying this is
the best building in the world

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:05.672
to walk into -- for
a show business job, especially.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:09.609
-Yes, it is. When I was here for
"SNL," I just loved getting up

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:13.312
onto the 8th floor and getting
into the studio and doing it.

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:15.749
And our offices
were on the 17th floor.

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:17.917
-Yes, 17, and then you do
the show on 8.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:20.386
And this was -- I think this is
the first thing

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:22.021
I was aware of you in.
-Right.

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:25.091
-Was "You Look Marvelous"
and "Fernando."

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:28.094
And this -- I did not realize,
you --

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:30.329
this was not heavily scripted.
-Not at all.

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:33.433
-Which is shocking to me,
because that was

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:35.834
beyond frowned upon in my time
at the show,

00:00:35.834 --> 00:00:37.103
but I guess it was
a different era.

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:39.305
-Yeah, I mean, Fernando
was a talk show host

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:42.608
who was wonderfully
underprepared.

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:45.110
-Yeah. So that helps the --
-Yeah.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:51.317
So whoever the guest host was
came into the hideaway with me.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:54.354
And we never rehearsed it,
we just put it on the air.

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:55.688
-Yeah.
-And I would just --

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.290
whatever happened, happened.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:58.891
-And were the guests game
for that?

00:00:58.891 --> 00:01:00.759
Did they -- I mean, they would
have had to have had an amazing

00:01:00.759 --> 00:01:01.894
amount of trust,
I would imagine.

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:03.662
-Yes. Some were terrified.
-Yeah.

00:01:03.662 --> 00:01:05.965
-Ringo -- Ringo was absolutely
terrified.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:10.102
His -- It was like his face was
like -- it was, like, beating.

00:01:10.102 --> 00:01:11.471
I remember looking at him.

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:14.073
So I ended up talking to Barbara
more than I talked to him.

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:17.109
But then one night --
and this is why live TV,

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:19.979
I just love it so much --

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:22.548
we were supposed to have --
Barry Manilow was supposed to be

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:24.184
the guest in the hideaway.

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:26.785
He was playing at Radio City
Music Hall across the street.

00:01:26.785 --> 00:01:30.556
At 11:10, he calls
and says he's not coming.

00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:32.926
He's too nervous to do it live.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.360
Can we script something for him?

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.962
And we said no.

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:38.131
We're 20 minutes away
from the air.

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:39.699
So we had a guy -- I don't know
if he was there

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:41.667
when you were there,
his name was Bobby Fraraccio.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:43.836
-I don't know if I know Bobby.
-Okay, you'd remember.

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:45.605
Bobby was a large man.
-Okay.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:49.108
-He was about 300, 400 pounds.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:53.246
-And he drove one of the cranes
in the studio.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:55.982
So -- And he had a great sense
of humor.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:57.250
So I went to him and I said,
"Bobby,

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.318
Manilow is not showing up."

00:01:59.318 --> 00:02:00.920
And goes, "That son of a --"
Bup-bup-bup.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.421
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.421 --> 00:02:06.225
"Would you play him and come
into the hideaway with me

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:09.462
and you'll be Barry Manilow?"

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:11.630
Because Fernando said
to the audience,

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:14.700
"I cannot disappoint my fans.
I cannot disappoint them.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:18.437
Barry Manilow did not show up,
but I promised you an interview

00:02:18.437 --> 00:02:19.972
with him and that's what we're
going to have."

00:02:19.972 --> 00:02:22.942
So -- now you saw him take
the headset off,

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.777
come into the hideaway.

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:28.113
I actually had to move the table
so he could come in,

00:02:28.113 --> 00:02:29.716
because he was so big.

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:32.986
And then I just interviewed him
as I would Barry, and it was --

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:35.821
he was hilarious.
He was absolutely hilarious.

00:02:35.821 --> 00:02:37.690
-And did you -- was the audience
on board with that

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:38.891
the minute it started?
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:40.393
Oh, yeah. They saw him.
That's -- you know.

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:43.462
And then I said -- I said to
Dick Ebersol, I said,

00:02:43.462 --> 00:02:46.833
"What if, for the rest of the
season, nobody shows up?"

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:48.768
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.036
"And it's always Bobby?"

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:51.670
-Yeah.
-"And it'll always be Bobby."

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:55.641
He goes, "No, no, no, Mr. C."
Mr. C. "I can't do it.

00:02:55.641 --> 00:02:57.609
My neighbors killed me,
my neighbors killed me.

00:02:57.609 --> 00:02:59.745
I can't do it, I can't do it."
-That's really funny.

00:02:59.745 --> 00:03:02.615
We once had a guest -- you know,
this is obviously the era

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:04.149
we live in,
where all of a sudden,

00:03:04.149 --> 00:03:06.185
somebody tests positive for
COVID and we don't have a guest.

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:08.053
And so, we had a whole hour
before the show.

00:03:08.053 --> 00:03:10.156
So we had our cue card guy,
Wally, came out here,

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:13.026
and I interviewed him -- as
Wally, it should be noted.

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:14.093
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:15.861
-But Wally was the opposite of
Bobby.

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:17.196
He wants to be interviewed
every week.

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:18.931
Like, I feel like --

00:03:18.931 --> 00:03:21.334
I feel like he's praying
people get COVID at this point.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.636
-And he was getting laughs.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:27.173
So during it I said, "So, it's
so lovely to have you here.

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:28.374
Why don't you sing us a song?"

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.109
And he started singing "I Write
the Songs,"

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:32.344
and he just started doing it.

00:03:32.344 --> 00:03:34.313
So I said, "We'll see you next
week," and I put my hand

00:03:34.313 --> 00:03:36.081
to stop him, and he just pushed
my hand away

00:03:36.081 --> 00:03:37.917
and kept singing the song.

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.118
-Yeah, classic Barry Manilow.

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:41.454
-No, he was the loveliest
of guys.

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:42.855
The loveliest of guys.
-And that was -- I mean,

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:44.991
you made quite an impact for
a very short period of time

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:46.592
on that show.
-We were only there a year.

00:03:46.592 --> 00:03:48.394
-Yeah.
-But, you know, look who we had.

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:51.764
Christopher Guest, Marty Short,
myself, Rich Hall,

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:53.866
Julia Louis-Dreyfus,
Jim Belushi.

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:55.768
-Did you know any of them ahead
of time?

00:03:55.768 --> 00:04:00.973
-Well, Marty and I and Chris,
yeah, and Harry, I knew.

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:03.375
And Rich Hall,
I knew a little bit,

00:04:03.375 --> 00:04:04.877
but I didn't know anybody else.

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:06.412
But I had hosted the year
before.

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:08.748
-Right.
-And -- twice, actually.

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:11.417
So I got to meet them then,

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:12.751
but that's different than
working with them.

00:04:12.751 --> 00:04:14.753
-That's a very surreal path,
to host the show

00:04:14.753 --> 00:04:16.289
and then get cast on it.

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:17.423
-Five months later.
-Yeah.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:18.924
-You know, Dick called that
summer and said,

00:04:18.924 --> 00:04:20.159
"Listen, we had such a good time
with you.

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:21.460
Would you think about it?"

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:24.430
I thought about it for about two
seconds and said, "Yeah."

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:27.800
-And in your head, was it always
gonna be a year?

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.369
-I thought I'd do it
for one year,

00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:32.037
but I sort of wanted to do it
more.

00:04:32.037 --> 00:04:33.706
And then a movie called
"Running Scared" happened

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:35.908
after that, and then that sort
of started to --

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:37.376
-With Gregory Hines?
Is that Gregory Hines?

00:04:37.376 --> 00:04:42.015
-Yeah. But as you know -- this
is exhausting, what I'm doing.

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:43.349
-Yeah.

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:45.751
-The "SNL" job
was even more tiring.

00:04:45.751 --> 00:04:48.553
-Yeah.
-We wrote, ourselves, a lot,

00:04:48.553 --> 00:04:49.756
you know? Marty and I.

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:53.392
And so one night --
this is a crazy story.

00:04:53.392 --> 00:04:57.030
It's, like, 3:00 am Tuesday,
read-through was Wednesday.

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:58.430
-Yep.
-Still? Yeah.

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:02.034
It's snowing really heavy,
and you're on the 17th floor,

00:05:02.034 --> 00:05:03.402
and you're looking out
over everything.

00:05:03.402 --> 00:05:05.971
I said, "I got to get home.
I got to get home."

00:05:05.971 --> 00:05:08.441
So Marty and I, we lived
downtown then.

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:10.643
We get in the cab and we're
driving down 7th Avenue.

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:12.744
We got to 33rd Street,
right near Penn Station.

00:05:12.744 --> 00:05:15.481
Red light. And we're talking
about how tired we are,

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:16.548
what are we going to do?

00:05:16.548 --> 00:05:19.218
And I hear an animal roar.

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:20.452
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.452 --> 00:05:21.921
Like a tiger, or --

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:24.323
Like [ Roaring ]

00:05:24.323 --> 00:05:26.992
And I went, "Marty,
what the hell was that?"

00:05:26.992 --> 00:05:30.963
And I look out the window and
through the condensation,

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:32.331
there's a tiger.

00:05:32.331 --> 00:05:33.899
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.899 --> 00:05:38.537
And I said, "I know I'm tired,
but are we seeing things?"

00:05:38.537 --> 00:05:40.439
And Marty goes, "What was it?"

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:44.376
The circus was loading into
Madison Square Garden,

00:05:44.376 --> 00:05:47.746
and they have all the animals
on chains and in cages

00:05:47.746 --> 00:05:51.951
loading across 7th Avenue,
coming off these huge trucks.

00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:55.555
And there they were in the snow,
just walking,

00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:57.490
and, you know,
with their time cards.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:58.858
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:01.761
"We'll be here for two weeks,
come and see us."

00:06:01.761 --> 00:06:03.629
It was the most bizarre thing
of all.

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:05.898
-I guess that is the --
I mean, people always say --

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:08.467
will ask me if I miss "SNL,"
and I always say,

00:06:08.467 --> 00:06:09.702
"I miss being that age."

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:11.871
Because I feel like, even though
I'm blown away

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:13.539
by what you're doing
every night,

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:15.607
and the fact that at your age,
you're doing a Broadway show.

00:06:15.607 --> 00:06:17.442
Like, I feel like there's
a certain time where you just

00:06:17.442 --> 00:06:19.045
age out of that "SNL" schedule.

00:06:19.045 --> 00:06:20.779
It's just impossible to do.
-It's just so hard.

00:06:20.779 --> 00:06:22.581
And for personal life,
it's just really hard.

00:06:22.581 --> 00:06:25.717
-Yeah.
-We're in rehearsal and --

00:06:25.717 --> 00:06:28.020
it's hard.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:31.123
And we're working -- you know,
I'm in eight songs

00:06:31.123 --> 00:06:33.860
and I have four dance numbers,
and it's thrilling.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:35.762
And I'm wearing
this Apple Watch, right,

00:06:35.762 --> 00:06:38.530
because I keep in great shape.
-Yeah.

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:41.734
-And so, I'm doing this number
and my wrist is buzzing.

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:44.303
What? What?
And so I look at it and it says

00:06:44.303 --> 00:06:45.571
"Have you fallen?"

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:48.441
[ Laughter ]

00:06:48.441 --> 00:06:50.142
And it lists the contacts
of the people

00:06:50.142 --> 00:06:52.011
that it wants to call.

00:06:52.011 --> 00:06:54.380
And it's got my wife and my kids
and my doctor.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:57.049
And I said, no -- I'm talking
about -- "No, I'm fine."

00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:59.285
Then it starts dialing,
because I'm supposed to, like,

00:06:59.285 --> 00:07:00.452
turn it off.

00:07:00.452 --> 00:07:01.754
And it kept saying,
"Have you fallen?

00:07:01.754 --> 00:07:02.988
Have you fallen?"

00:07:02.988 --> 00:07:04.923
-And you're like, "Fallen?
I'm Tony-nominated!"

00:07:04.923 --> 00:07:06.392
-Right.
-I'm on the way up!

00:07:06.392 --> 00:07:09.194
-And I can get up.
I've fallen and I can get up.

00:07:09.194 --> 00:07:11.330
-Hey, congratulations
on the show

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:12.798
and all the nominations.

00:07:12.798 --> 00:07:13.866
What an honor to have you here.
-Good to be here. Thank you.

00:07:13.866 --> 00:07:16.802
-Billy Crystal.
"Mr. Saturday Night"

00:07:16.802 --> 00:07:18.938
is playing at the
Nederlander Theater on Broadway.

00:07:18.938 --> 00:07:20.373
We'll be right back with
Samara Weaving.

